            "runtimes": [
              {
                "asset": {
                  "content": "# Eve runtime boundary\n\nThe `support` agent uses the nested Eve filesystem layout at `/agent`. Its canonical static surfaces are `/agent/agent.ts`, exact lowercase `/agent/instructions.md`, the output schema in `/agent/contracts.ts`, the `status` `defineTool` module, and the `triage` TypeScript `defineSkill` module.\n\nSupported static alternatives are a flat or nested root `agent.ts`; one exact lowercase `instructions.md` or statically analyzable `instructions.ts`; recursive TypeScript `defineTool` modules; TypeScript `defineSkill` modules; direct schema relationships; and directory-backed local subagents at `subagents/<name>/agent.ts` with separately registered canonical agents and evidenced routing.\n\nSource presence alone does not establish dynamic tools, flat or packaged Markdown skills, single-file subagents, or case-varied, composed, and legacy instruction forms. Remote agents, extension contributions, connection and framework tools, filesystem collisions, reserved names, and advanced runtime behavior likewise require runtime evidence or a supported static form before they become canonical. This guide asserts no provider or model behavior.\n",
                  "digest": "sha256:21bb3251ce41e2518f87e992a267b57627c853054e96a6c531b7e1376482e6be",
                  "path": "/moldea/runtimes/eve.md",
                  "scalarLength": 1162,
                  "utf8ByteLength": 1162
                }
              }
            ],
